@digiexchris I used the modification to the driver in the #72107 along with the sample located at [`samples/drivers/display`](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/tree/main/samples/drivers/display).

Instead of a DT overlay, I used a `SYS_INIT` function in the directory for my (not-yet-upstreamed) board that calls `display_set_orientation(..., DISPLAY_ORIENTATION_ROTATED_180)` at startup.

```c
int esp32s3_t_watch_display_on(void)
{
	// Set the orientation
	const struct device *display = DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_CHOSEN(zephyr_display));
	if (!device_is_ready(display))
	{
		return -EIO;
	}

	int ret = display_set_orientation(display, DISPLAY_ORIENTATION_ROTATED_180);
	if (ret < 0)
	{
		return ret;
	}

	return 0;
}

SYS_INIT(esp32s3_t_watch_display_on, APPLICATION, CONFIG_APPLICATION_INIT_PRIORITY);
```
